  "entry": "code/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A Streamlit toolkit for glioblastoma drug discovery, with a stated target focus on the CDC25A/B/C phosphatases. It screens SMILES for drug-likeness and blood-brain-barrier penetration, validates and runs AutoDock Vina docking, fits IC50 curves, and runs Kaplan-Meier, log-rank and docking-enrichment statistics. It also does differential expression and co-expression on expression tables. Every output is labelled by its source. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
